# Endpoint Rules

## Router file structure

```python
from __future__ import annotations

from fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, status
from sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession

from app.dependencies.db import get_db
from app.schemas.my_schema import MyRequest, MyResponse
from app.services.my_service import MyService

router = APIRouter()


@router.post(
    "",
    response_model=MyResponse,
    status_code=status.HTTP_201_CREATED,
    summary="Short summary shown in docs",
)
async def create_thing(
    payload: MyRequest,
    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db),
) -> MyResponse:
    service = MyService(db)
    return await service.create(payload)
```

## Checklist for every endpoint
- `response_model` always set
- `status_code` explicit (not relying on 200 default)
- `summary` set for OpenAPI docs
- Router calls exactly ONE service method
- No business logic in the router function body
- Protected endpoints use `CurrentUserID` from `app.dependencies.auth`
